ent-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>58073994</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-8288069-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>8288069</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1117277A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit><nplcit status="new"><text>SHIZUO TOKITO ET AL.: 'Metal oxides as a hole-injecting layer for an organic electroluminescent device' J. PHYS. D; APPL. PHYS. vol. 29, 1996, pages 2750 - 2753, XP002926350</text><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TDK CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TDK CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ARAI MICHIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ARAI, MICHIO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An organic EL device having merits which organic materials and inorganic material have, a high efficiency, and a long life, and produced at low cost, comprising a couple of a hole injection electrode (2) and an electron injection electrode (6), an organic layer (4) provided between the electrodes (2, 6), concerning a light-emitting function, and including a light-emitting layer containing a conjugated polymer, and an inorganic hole injection layer (3) provided between the organic layer (4) and the hole injection electrode (2), including a conductive path for blocking electrons and for transporting holes, and having a high resistance.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un dispositif EL organique présentant les avantages liés aux matériaux organiques et inorganiques, à haut rendement ainsi qu'une durée de vie prolongée, produit à faible coût, comprenant un couple d'une électrode d'injection (2) à trous et d'une électrode d'injection (6) d'électrons, une couche organique (4) ménagée entre les électrodes (2, 6), concernant une fonction luminescente, et contenant une couche luminescente renfermant un polymère conjugué, ainsi qu'une couche d'injection (3) à trous inorganique ménagée entre la couche organique (4) et l'électrode d'injection (2) à trous, renfermant un chemin conducteur destiné à bloquer les électrons et à transporter les trous, et présentant une résistance élevée.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>